### Bug Scenario and Root Cause

The bug occurs when using `rel="noopener"` on `mailto:` links. The `mailto:` link with `rel="noopener"` fails to open the email client on Chrome for Android and iOS Safari, resulting in a blank page. The link without `rel="noopener"` works correctly and opens the email client. This issue arises because `rel="noopener"` is not necessary for `mailto:` links and causes them to break on certain mobile browsers.

### Bug Location and Fix

The issue is in the `lighthouse-core/audits/dobetterweb/external-anchors-use-rel-noopener.js` file. The audit should ignore `mailto:` links when checking for `rel="noopener"`.

